{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-15T07:09:59.771Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489731d8ab76ae02b28618d0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1336"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1336: a claim held by an ended agent blocks everyone until --force; refusals and pm next omit its age and last activity, and no policy permits a stale takeover"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1336 (filed 2026-09-28) reports claims left behind by ended agents across nine repositories. Today a held item refuses pm claim with already_claimed_by, which carries claimed_by, claimed_at and claim_source but neither the last recorded activity nor how long the item has been idle. pm next lists foreign work under held_by_others as bare {id, assignee} rows. The only way past an abandoned claim is --force, which takes over an active claim just as readily, so agents either wait forever or override work in progress. This tranche of pm-szv11n delivers the standalone claim criteria from that story: holder, claim age and last activity in the refusal and the next-item occupancy view, an explicit stale-claim policy that permits a conditional takeover without --force, and auditable takeover history. The inactivity clock is the item's last recorded mutation (max of updated_at and the newest history entry), and the threshold is the existing mutation_guard.stale_in_progress_hours setting that pm health already uses for stale in-progress work, so the item health calls stale is the item a takeover may claim. The cross-branch claim race (GH-1406) and the merge-composition scenarios stay on pm-szv11n. Duplicate check: searched claim takeover stale dead agent, read pm-szv11n, pm-8t5x, pm-05u4, pm-w9w4, pm-d4bo, pm-gh1706 and pm-1wujzi (bulk occupancy derived state, not per-item diagnostics); none owns the standalone stale-takeover tranche."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","claims","gh:1336","multi-agent","ownership","stale-work"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-15T07:09:59.771Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-15T07:09:59.771Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The already_claimed_by refusal reports the holder, claimed_at, claim_age_hours, last_activity_at, idle_hours and the stale-claim policy (threshold_hours, the setting key, whether the claim is stale and when it becomes eligible), computed under the item lock; pm next held_by_others rows report claimed_at, last_activity_at, idle_hours and stale while reading at most one history stream per returned row; pm claim <id> --takeover-stale takes over a non-terminal claim only when its idle time meets mutation_guard.stale_in_progress_hours, refuses an active or too-recent claim with stale_claim_takeover_refused and no mutation, behaves as a plain claim for an unclaimed or self-held item, and is refused in combination with --force or --next; A permitted takeover records previous_holder, new_holder, last_activity_at, idle_hours, threshold_hours and the policy key in the claim history entry's structured context, and the claim result carries the same takeover receipt; Isolated CLI, SDK and MCP scenarios cover active, stale, released, unclaimed and renewed claims, including a claim renewed after a refusal being refused again on retry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-szv11n"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An agent meeting another agent's claim sees how long that claim has been idle, and can take over an abandoned claim under an explicit policy that refuses active ones, with the takeover recorded in history."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The refusal and pm next omit last activity and idle time, and --force is the only takeover path, which overrides active claims as readily as abandoned ones."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0f92e0b57a687051fa983db6bb53c0fe42ca2559a3a78a3b26fe743b570b6a8e","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8a629c9b0ba5327f546f34e5db4209fa28fa2df7eef4c62549eecb90bd8601e0"}
